{
  "dom_id": "step-e2280",
  "name": "Example: Calculating an Amount Given a Ratio as a Fraction",
  "problem": "Noah has $42$ toy blocks, of which $\\dfrac{5}{7}$ are blue, and the rest are green. How many green blocks does Noah have?",
  "worked_solution": "Explanation:\n\nWe are given that the ratio of blue blocks to the total number of blocks is $\\dfrac{{\\color{blue}5}}{{\\color{red}7}}.$ \n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of blue blocks, and the denominator represents   the total number of blocks .\n\nWe can make a denominator of $42$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $6{:}$\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{\\color{blue}5}\\times 6}{{\\color{red}7}\\times 6} = \\dfrac{{\\color{blue}30}}{{\\color{red}42}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are $30$ blue blocks. \n\nSo the number of green blocks is\n\n$$\n42 - 30 = 12.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
